      {
        "text": "Tina Simone McKinnor represents the 61st District in the California State Assembly, where she has served since 2022. She previously worked as a civic engagement director and chief of staff to several Assembly members. McKinnor chairs the Assembly Public Employment and Retirement Committee and the Select Committee on Restorative Justice.",
        "cites": [1, 2],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Tina Simone McKinnor represents the 61st District in the California State Assembly, where she has served since 2022.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She previously worked as a civic engagement director and chief of staff to several Assembly members.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "McKinnor chairs the Assembly Public Employment and Retirement Committee and the Select Committee on Restorative Justice.",
            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "She authored the bill that let legislative staff unionize. She introduced measures to allow resentencing for people with gun enhancements, expand youth offender parole, and ensure restorative justice program integrity. She wrote a bill ending mandatory police reporting of suspected domestic violence victims. According to CalMatters, she authored an AT&T-sponsored bill to phase out most landlines and pledged to reintroduce it.",
        "cites": [3, 4, 5],
